09</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B12"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Adlassnig</surname><given-names>KP</given-names></name><name><surname>Combi</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Das</surname><given-names>AK</given-names></name><name><surname>Keravnou</surname><given-names>ET</given-names></name><name><surname>Pozzi</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Temporal representation and reasoning in medicine: Research directions and challenges</article-title><source>Artif Intell Med</source><year>2006</year><volume>38</volume><fpage>101</fpage><lpage>113</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17081736</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/j.artmed.2006.10.001</pub-id></citation></ref></ref-list></back></article>